.TH MOCHAD-REDUX-SETUP 8
.SH NAME
mochad-redux-setup \- administer native mochad-redux integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mochad-redux-setup
.I command
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The setup tool explicitly creates the native service account and renders the
inactive templates installed by the package.  Package installation itself never
performs these host changes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Create accounts and install managed systemd and udev integration.
.TP
.B verify
Verify managed files and selected service settings.
.TP
.B status
Display the resolved paths and current integration status.
.TP
.B remove
Remove managed integration files.  It preserves configuration and accounts.
.TP
.B purge
Explicit destructive cleanup.  Account removal additionally requires
.BR --purge-accounts .
.SH OPTIONS
.BR --enable , " --enable-now" , " --restart" , " --no-systemd" ,
.BR --no-udev , " --service-user" , " --service-group" , " --usb-group" ,
.BR --prefix , " --dry-run" , " --force"
are supported.  Run with
.B --help
for details.
